# Quantum proposal development lock

The **Quantum** proposal (`residential_quantum`, Cinematic Neo-Glass renderer) is **complete and locked for development**.

## What "locked" means

- **Do NOT** modify Quantum proposal files when fixing or building **other** presets (Golden, Luxe, Sales Premium, Ember, Horizon, Solstice, Legacy, Commercial, etc.).
- **Do NOT** hide or disable other themes in the UI — users may still choose any template.
- **Only** edit Quantum when the user **explicitly** asks to change the Quantum proposal.

## Frozen paths (no edits unless user requests Quantum changes)

- `components/QuantumPreset/**`
- `components/proposals/_registry/adapters/quantum-adapter.tsx`

See also `lib/quantum-proposal-lock.ts`.

## Separation from other proposals

- Quantum lives in its **own** folder and CSS module — not Golden editorial, not Luxe-noir pages.
- Other presets must not import Quantum CSS/components to “share” look; duplicate or adapt locally if needed.
- Do not refactor shared Golden/Luxe utilities for Quantum’s sake (or the reverse).
- Shared `ProposalData` / branding / formatters may feed Quantum; keep those changes lane-safe and do not break `residential_quantum` rendering.

## When working on other presets

- Scope diffs to that preset’s blocks, CSS, and registry entries only.
- Do not change Quantum glass, motion, i18n, or A4 pages to match another theme.

## Public route

Quantum renders at `preset_id === "residential_quantum"` via `QuantumAdapter` → `QuantumRenderer` — keep that path stable.
